          {
            "id": "H003",
            "statement": "R>0.",
            "origin": "problem.md:88; target-selection.json/full_target"
          }
        ],
        "conclusion": "There exist positive constants C and tau0 depending only on T,gamma,R such that, for every real mean-zero u0 in H^gamma(Ttor) with ||u0||_(H^gamma)<=R and every positive integer L with tau=T/L<=tau0, the exact KdV solution in D012 exists and the unmodified unfiltered scheme D009–D011 is well defined and satisfies max_(0<=n<=L)||u(n*tau)-u^n||_(L2)<=C*tau^gamma. These constants are uniform on the entire initial-data ball, all permitted timesteps, and all Fourier supports, with the domain, normalized measure, Fourier/Sobolev conventions, Airy group, projections, inverse derivatives and full Ftau,Htau formula fixed in D001–D012."
